fetlock
=======

A shoeing log for the ankle-anklet work: the code that backs our sex-aware,
transfer-learned screen for post-traumatic ankle osteoarthritis (PTOA) running on
a wrist-to-ankle accelerometer/gyroscope stream and ending on a Cortex-M4F class
microcontroller. The same tree also carries the offline neuro-biomechanical
concordance check that ties wearable-derived gait primitives to literature-reported
cortical activation.

The pipeline has four legs, kept in the package as separate craft areas:

  paddock    six-axis windowing, the planted-signal cohort, subject-stratified
             splits with no window leakage, and the pretext augmentations
  forge      the temporal CNN spine, the three pretext heads, the shared body
             with male/female routing, the depthwise-separable student, and the
             min-max INT8 press
  temper     the pretraining objective (temporal-order + transform + NT-Xent),
             the sex-aware loss with cross-head KL, and the distillation loss
  soundness  AUC / F1 / sensitivity / specificity, fast DeLong, paired bootstrap,
             Holm-Bonferroni, Benjamini-Hochberg, partial eta-squared, kappa,
             permutation, ECE, and the feature-to-ROI concordance panel
  shoeing    seeding, atomic checkpoints, AdamW + warmup-cosine, early stopping,
             grad-accumulation training loop, DDP wiring
  farrier    the command-line bench

What the four legs correspond to in the write-up: Eq. (1) is the pretraining
objective, Eq. (2) the sex-aware loss, Eq. (3) the temperature-scaled distillation,
Eq. (4) the anchor-resampled Pearson concordance. Stage routing sends a known-sex
window to its matched head and averages both heads when sex is unknown.


Setting up
----------

pip:

    python -m venv .venv && . .venv/bin/activate
    pip install -r requirements.txt
    pip install -e .

conda:

    conda env create -f environment.yml
    conda activate fetlock
    pip install -e . --no-deps

docker:

    docker build -t fetlock .
    docker run --rm --gpus all fetlock finetune --job dockets/jobs/main.toml

The pin is deliberate and unfriendly: CUDA 11.7, torch 1.13.1, Python 3.8. The
profile in dockets/jobs/main.toml is the one we actually ran, not a laptop-sized
shortcut. dockets/jobs/_bench.toml exists only so the vetting suite can move two
steps in a second; do not report anything from it.


Data
----

Every corpus and every neuro anchor lives in forage.txt with its access route and
licence. MOST and OAI are controlled access; CGWS and GaitRec are CC-BY on figshare;
the UK Biobank accelerometer corpus and the released self-supervised encoder back the
pretraining leg. No raw fMRI is touched -- the concordance leg consumes published
effect sizes only.

A prepared cohort is a directory with manifest.jsonl plus the per-subject .npy
arrays; point data_root at it. With no manifest present the bench falls back to the
planted-signal cohort so the commands stay runnable end to end.


Running the bench
-----------------

    fetlock pretrain    --job dockets/jobs/pretrain.toml
    fetlock adapt       --job dockets/jobs/adapt.toml
    fetlock finetune    --job dockets/jobs/main.toml
    fetlock distill     --job dockets/jobs/distill.toml
    fetlock evaluate    --job dockets/jobs/main.toml
    fetlock concordance --job dockets/jobs/main.toml
    fetlock export-onnx --job dockets/jobs/distill.toml --out artifacts/anklet_student.onnx

Any leaf of the config is reachable from the command line:

    fetlock finetune --job dockets/jobs/main.toml --set optim.lr=1e-6 --set schedule.epochs=2000

The ablations in Table II and the input-channel study sit beside the main job:
ablation_no_tl, ablation_no_sex, ablation_no_da, ablation_sex_as_feature,
ablation_accel_only, ablation_gyro_only. The transfer-fraction and cross-dataset
sweeps are the supplementary_* jobs. rounds/ holds the torchrun and sweep wrappers.


What to expect
--------------

On MOST, the routed full model lands near AUC 0.934 +/- 0.016 over the ten seeds
{42, 123, 256, 512, 789, 1024, 1337, 2048, 3141, 4096}, about 3.3 pp over the next
baseline; the female subgroup gains about 5.2 pp over sex-mixed training. The
INT8 student is reported at 48 KB and 12 ms per ten-second window with ~98.9 percent
of teacher accuracy. The concordance panel recovers SMA-dorsiflexion at r = 0.43
(p = 0.007) and M1-plantarflexion at r = 0.38 (p = 0.018), surviving FDR; stride-time
with S1 and ankle-ROM with cerebellum sit at the FDR boundary. These are
literature-anchored, hypothesis-generating numbers, not subject-matched claims.


Compute budget
--------------

Eight A100-80GB. The finetune and pretrain jobs carry an effective batch of
8 x 256 x 24 = 49152 at fp32, learning rate 2e-7, warmup-cosine over 4000 epochs,
weight decay 1e-2, gradient clip 1.0. Distillation runs at temperature 4.0 with
alpha 0.7 and an INT8 calibration set of 500 windows drawn min-max. Walking this in
fp32 at the stated effective batch needs the full eight-card node; it is not a
single-GPU afternoon.


Checkpoints
-----------

Encoder and student weights are available on reasonable request. Checkpoints are
written atomically and carry the seed and RNG state, so a resumed run continues the
same stream it started.
